  "body": "Part of #363 (research comment there has the sources and the safety reasoning).\n\nPriority: P1 (correctness of the verification claim; not a gouge)\n\nWith `G76Cycle`, the explicit passes have to match the control's own schedule: Δd·√n clamped at Δdmin, finish allowance d, m-1 spring passes, tool angle a as modified flank. The record maps 1:1 to `P(m)(r)(a) Q R` / `P(k) Q(Δd)`. Anything the cycle cannot express is refused by name: alternating infeed, per-depth repeats, dips, angles outside 0/29/30/55/60/80.\n*Done means:* a golden G76 test where the simulated pass depths equal the control's √n sequence for the same words, plus a refusal test per unexpressible option. Depends on (a).\n",
